          "type": "text",
          "text": "About this pattern"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A grey diplodocus with a wide oval body, a very long cylinder neck, a very long tapered cylinder tail, and a small sphere head. The diplodocus is longer than a brachiosaurus but lower to the ground, so the neck extends forward rather than straight up. Fill the neck with stuffing as you work each section."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Body"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Rounds: 23. Begin with a "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "glossaryTooltip",
              "attrs": {
                "termSlug": "magic-ring"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "magic ring"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "glossaryTooltip",
              "attrs": {
                "termSlug": "amigurumi-increase"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "increase"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to the widest point, work straight, then "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "glossaryTooltip",
              "attrs": {
                "termSlug": "amigurumi-decrease"
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "decrease"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " toward the tail end. Stuff firmly and close."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Round 1: Chain 21. Working along chain: 2 sc in 2nd ch from hook, sc in next 18 ch, 3 sc in last ch, rotate. Along opposite side: sc in next 18 ch, 2 sc in last ch (44 st)"
        }
      ]
    },
